      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When drafting a Master Service Agreement with a raw material supplier in Munich, consider including standard terms and conditions such as:\n\n* Payment terms, including net payment, invoice discount, and late payment fees\n* Delivery and availability commitments, including minimum order quantities and lead times\n* Pricing stabilization clauses, such as fixed or variable pricing, padding, or market-linked adjustments\n* Supply chain resilience provisions, including supply insurance, performance guarantees, and sourcing diversification\n* Currency conversion and hedging clauses\n* Non-disclosure and confidentiality agreements\n* Termination and breach provisions, with notice periods and resolution procedures\n* Dispute resolution mechanisms, including arbitration and mediation \n\nKeep in mind that this is not an exhaustive list and you should adjust it according to your company's specific needs and industry requirements.",
